ord":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"Status unverified in this edition: no build or extraction receipt of this tool binds it.","citation_ids":["cite.lean.QuarticQuery.theorem_1_1_unconditional"],"declaration":"QuarticQuery.theorem_1_1_unconditional","evidence_ids":[],"id":"lean.QuarticQuery.theorem_1_1_unconditional","kind":"declaration","label":"QuarticQuery.theorem_1_1_unconditional","locator":"QuarticQuery/Results/Unconditional.lean, line 23","source_id":"lean:QuarticQuery/Results/Unconditional.lean","statement":"QuarticQuery.theorem_1_1_unconditional","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/nodes/lean.QuarticQuery.theorem_1_1_unconditional","table":"nodes","usage":{"direct_passages":[],"paper_focus":[],"paper_memberships":[{"roles":["recorded_prerequisite"],"stage":"long","subgraph_ref":"sha256:5575b8b556fd70f82bee36584a279e50d338cd389fbc4d6892ab977a211acfca/papers/long.json/support/0.3.1/d4eb68d364337362a2c46b483a435f86d7d0d580d15f024a6af37a3d07ef2dce"},{"roles":["recorded_prerequisite"],"stage":"short","subgraph_ref":"sha256:f6eb3589d952604396c173f3a132039ec1cedbbc57b65f184e1ca67bee914b6b/papers/short.json/support/0.3.1/f9c8348dc1f401cbae8afaedd41f18345751689e6b6298e453c9c48169cf6257"},{"roles":["recorded_prerequisite"],"stage":"expository","subgraph_ref":"sha256:0e0b8ed54de434b100596a9e6374160bfb146bc7905b31307a73825c7034dd44/papers/expository.json/support/0.3.1/f7125c873525eba045c0c24a8bb99ad310a22459dfeb43eb1884a5c1dd02931f"}],"record_ref":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/nodes/lean.QuarticQuery.theorem_1_1_unconditional"}},{"href":"/api/v1/record?manifest=c02ee087719f86b306aeb0592c0b7c61d641c5fb7814a548b94e0b3be06311d2&ref=sha256%3Ab01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40%2Fnodes%2Fquartic.lemma-2","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"A result as the authors number it. Its links to the Lean were made with AI for Proof Reader and have not been reviewed by the authors.","citation_ids":["cite.quartic.lemma-2"],"evidence_ids":["link.quartic.lemma-2"],"id":"quartic.lemma-2","kind":"claim","label":"Lemma 2","locator":"Lemma 2, Section 2","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Lemma 2** (OpenAI ([OpenAI 2026](#cite-OpenAI2026), Lemma 2.1)). *Fix $k\\ge2$. For all sufficiently large powers of four $m$,*\n$$\n L:=\\left\\lfloor m^{1-1/k}/\\ell^2\\right\\rfloor < R(P).\n\\tag{3}\n$$\n*For every $0<\\eta<1/2$ a reversible quantum algorithm with $O_k(1+\\log(1/\\eta))$ queries on every input computes $P$ with error at most $\\eta$ on its domain. There is an exact fan-in-two circuit with $S=O_k(m\\ell^2)$ gates whose two outputs are the domain bit of $P$ and, on the domain, its value.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/nodes/quartic.lemma-2","table":"nodes","usage":{"direct_passages":[{"anchor":"sec-2","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:f6eb3589d952604396c173f3a132039ec1cedbbc57b65f184e1ca67bee914b6b/papers/short.json","passage_ref":"sha256:62ba85c0268de6b2c3c184bdaa0f57be2fe0e4a4de54a371d1db80fabd64829a/papers/short.md/sha256:f6eb3589d952604396c173f3a132039ec1cedbbc57b65f184e1ca67bee914b6b/papers/short.json/passages/sec-2","stage":"short"}],"paper_focus":[],"paper_memberships":[{"roles":["mapped_claim"],"stage":"short","subgraph_ref":"sha256:f6eb3589d952604396c173f3a132039ec1cedbbc57b65f184e1ca67bee914b6b/papers/short.json/support/0.3.1/f9c8348dc1f401cbae8afaedd41f18345751689e6b6298e453c9c48169cf6257"}],"record_ref":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/nodes/quartic.lemma-2"}},{"href":"/api/v1/record?manifest=c02ee087719f86b306aeb0592c0b7c61d641c5fb7814a548b94e0b3be06311d2&ref=sha256%3Ab01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40%2Fnodes%2Fquartic.lemma-4","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"A result as the authors number it. Its links to the Lean were made with AI for Proof Reader and have not been reviewed by the authors.","citation_ids":["cite.quartic.lemma-4"],"evidence_ids":["link.quartic.lemma-4"],"id":"quartic.lemma-4","kind":"claim","label":"Lemma 4","locator":"Lemma 4, Section 4.2","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Lemma 4** (bounded amplification ([OpenAI 2026](#cite-OpenAI2026), Lemma 3.1); see @BBHT1998 and @BHMT2002). *Let $A$ prepare a state with a success flag, with success probability $p$. For $0<\\gamma\\le1/2$ and $0<\\eta<1/2$ there is a procedure making $O(\\gamma^{-1/2}\\log(1/\\eta))$ calls to $A$ and $A^{-1}$ on every branch, for every $p$, that either reports failure or produces a successful outcome. Conditional on success, the measured label has the same distribution as in the successful part of $A$'s state. If $p\\ge\\gamma$ it fails with probability at most $\\eta$, and if $p=0$ it always fails.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/nodes/quartic.lemma-4","table":"nodes","usage":{"direct_passages":[{"anchor":"sec-4","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:f6eb3589d952604396c173f3a132039ec1cedbbc57b65f184e1ca67bee914b6b/papers/short.json","passage_ref":"sha256:62ba85c0268de6b2c3c184bdaa0f57be2fe0e4a4de54a371d1db80fabd64829a/papers/short.md/sha256:f6eb3589d952604396c173f3a132039ec1cedbbc57b65f184e1ca67bee914b6b/papers/short.json/passages/sec-4","stage":"short"}],"paper_focus":[],"paper_memberships":[{"roles":["mapped_claim"],"stage":"short","subgraph_ref":"sha256:f6eb3589d952604396c173f3a132039ec1cedbbc57b65f184e1ca67bee914b6b/papers/short.json/support/0.3.1/f9c8348dc1f401cbae8afaedd41f18345751689e6b6298e453c9c48169cf6257"}],"record_ref":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/nodes/quartic.lemma-4"}},{"href":"/api/v1/record?manifest=c02ee087719f86b306aeb0592c0b7c61d641c5fb7814a548b94e0b3be06311d2&ref=sha256%3Ab01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40%2Fnodes%2Fquartic.lemma-5","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"A result as the authors number it. Its links to the Lean were made with AI for Proof Reader and have not been reviewed by the authors.","citation_ids":["cite.quartic.lemma-5"],"evidence_ids":["link.quartic.lemma-5"],"id":"quartic.lemma-5","kind":"claim","label":"Lemma 5","locator":"Lemma 5, Section 5.3","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Lemma 5** (OpenAI ([OpenAI 2026](#cite-OpenAI2026), Lemma 4.1); @Shaltiel2003; @Drucker2012). *Let $P$ be a partial function and $\\mu$ a distribution on its domain such that every deterministic algorithm making at most $L$ queries computes $P$ under $\\mu$ with probability at most $\\beta$. If $U_1,\\ldots,U_r$ are independent samples from $\\mu$, every algorithm making at most $L$ queries to each $U_h$ outputs $(P(U_1),\\ldots,P(U_r))$ with probability at most $\\beta^r$. The algorithm may be randomized, interleave its queries adaptively among the $r$ inputs, and receive additional information independent of $(U_1,\\ldots,U_r)$.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/nodes/quartic.lemma-5","table":"nodes","usage":{"direct_passages":[{"anchor":"sec-5","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:f6eb3589d952604396c173f3a132039ec1cedbbc57b65f184e1ca67bee914b6b/papers/short.json","passage_ref":"sha256:62ba85c0268de6b2c3c184bdaa0f57be2fe0e4a4de54a371d1db80fabd64829a/papers/short.md/sha256:f6eb3589d952604396c173f3a132039ec1cedbbc57b65f184e1ca67bee914b6b/papers/short.json/passages/sec-5","stage":"short"}],"paper_focus":[],"paper_memberships":[{"roles":["mapped_claim"],"stage":"short","subgraph_ref":"sha256:f6eb3589d952604396c173f3a132039ec1cedbbc57b65f184e1ca67bee914b6b/papers/short.json/support/0.3.1/f9c8348dc1f401cbae8afaedd41f18345751689e6b6298e453c9c48169cf6257"}],"record_ref":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/nodes/quartic.lemma-5"}},{"href":"/api/v1/record?manifest=c02ee087719f86b306aeb0592c0b7c61d641c5fb7814a548b94e0b3be06311d2&ref=sha256%3Ab01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40%2Fnodes%2Fquartic.proposition-3","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"A result as the authors number it. Its links to the Lean were made with AI for Proof Reader and have not been reviewed by the authors.","citation_ids":["cite.quartic.proposition-3"],"evidence_ids":["link.quartic.proposition-3"],"id":"quartic.proposition-3","kind":"claim","label":"Proposition 3","locator":"Proposition 3, Section 4.2","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Proposition 3** (OpenAI ([OpenAI 2026](#cite-OpenAI2026), Proposition 3.2)). *Let $T=\\lceil\\log(1000m)\\rceil$ and $\\varepsilon=1/(1000T)$. Suppose a reversible comparison circuit, controlled by two candidate indices, uses at most $c$ queries and satisfies (4). There is a quantum algorithm making $O(c\\sqrt m\\,T^2\\log T)$ queries on every branch and returning a list of at most $T$ candidates such that, if $a_{i^\\star j}\\ge1-\\varepsilon$ for all $j\\ne i^\\star$, the list contains $i^\\star$ with probability at least $1-2m2^{-T}-T\\varepsilon$.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/nodes/quartic.proposition-3","table":"nodes","usage":{"direct_passages":[{"anchor":"sec-4","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:f6eb3589d952604396c173f3a132039ec1cedbbc57b65f184e1ca67bee914b6b/papers/short.json","passage_ref":"sha256:62ba85c0268de6b2c3c184bdaa0f57be2fe0e4a4de54a371d1db80fabd64829a/papers/short.md/sha256:f6eb3589d952604396c173f3a132039ec1cedbbc57b65f184e1ca67bee914b6b/papers/short.json/passages/sec-4","stage":"short"}],"paper_focus":[],"paper_memberships":[{"roles":["mapped_claim"],"stage":"short","subgraph_ref":"sha256:f6eb3589d952604396c173f3a132039ec1cedbbc57b65f184e1ca67bee914b6b/papers/short.json/support/0.3.1/f9c8348dc1f401cbae8afaedd41f18345751689e6b6298e453c9c48169cf6257"}],"record_ref":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/nodes/quartic.proposition-3"}},{"href":"/api/v1/record?manifest=c02ee087719f86b306aeb0592c0b7c61d641c5fb7814a548b94e0b3be06311d2&ref=sha256%3Ab01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40%2Fnodes%2Fquartic.theorem-1","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"A result as the authors number it. Its links to the Lean were made with AI for Proof Reader and have not been reviewed by the authors.","citation_ids":["cite.quartic.theorem-1"],"evidence_ids":["link.quartic.theorem-1"],"id":"quartic.theorem-1","kind":"goal","label":"Theorem 1","locator":"Theorem 1, Section 1","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Theorem 1** (OpenAI ([OpenAI 2026](#cite-OpenAI2026), Theorem 1.1)). *For every total Boolean function $f$, $R(f)=O((1+Q(f))^4)$. For each fixed integer $k\\ge2$ there are positive constants $c_k$, $C_k$ and $b_k$ and total Boolean functions $F_{k,m}$, defined for powers of four $m$, such that for all sufficiently large $m$, with $\\ell=\\log_2m$,*\n$$\n Q(F_{k,m})\\le C_k\\sqrt m\\,\\ell^{b_k},\n \\qquad R(F_{k,m})\\ge c_k\\,\\frac{m^{2-1/k}}{\\ell^2}.\n\\tag{1}\n$$\n*Consequently the critical exponent of $R$ relative to $Q$ is four.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/nodes/quartic.theorem-1","table":"nodes","usage":{"direct_passages":[{"anchor":"front","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:5575b8b556fd70f82bee36584a279e50d338cd389fbc4d6892ab977a211acfca/papers/long.json","passage_ref":"sha256:806053e019b394fdff0c88914564f8211e037c58b65d06b8bf0cea131d4863c0/papers/long.md/sha256:5575b8b556fd70f82bee36584a279e50d338cd389fbc4d6892ab977a211acfca/papers/long.json/passages/front","stage":"long"},{"anchor":"sec-1","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:f6eb3589d952604396c173f3a132039ec1cedbbc57b65f184e1ca67bee914b6b/papers/short.json","passage_ref":"sha256:62ba85c0268de6b2c3c184bdaa0f57be2fe0e4a4de54a371d1db80fabd64829a/papers/short.md/sha256:f6eb3589d952604396c173f3a132039ec1cedbbc57b65f184e1ca67bee914b6b/papers/short.json/passages/sec-1","stage":"short"},{"anchor":"front","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:0e0b8ed54de434b100596a9e6374160bfb146bc7905b31307a73825c7034dd44/papers/expository.json","passage_ref":"sha256:359d7ed5dc9dd8decc0557661fdee98a6d01f51717c30dafd2bd0188e6e21927/papers/expository.md/sha256:0e0b8ed54de434b100596a9e6374160bfb146bc7905b31307a73825c7034dd44/papers/expository.json/passages/front","stage":"expository"}],"paper_focus":[{"mapping_ref":"sha256:5575b8b556fd70f82bee36584a279e50d338cd389fbc4d6892ab977a211acfca/papers/long.json","stage":"long"},{"mapping_ref":"sha256:f6eb3589d952604396c173f3a132039ec1cedbbc57b65f184e1ca67bee914b6b/papers/short.json","stage":"short"},{"mapping_ref":"sha256:0e0b8ed54de434b100596a9e6374160bfb146bc7905b31307a73825c7034dd44/papers/expository.json","stage":"expository"}],"paper_memberships":[{"roles":["mapped_claim"],"stage":"long","subgraph_ref":"sha256:5575b8b556fd70f82bee36584a279e50d338cd389fbc4d6892ab977a211acfca/papers/long.json/support/0.3.1/d4eb68d364337362a2c46b483a435f86d7d0d580d15f024a6af37a3d07ef2dce"},{"roles":["mapped_claim"],"stage":"short","subgraph_ref":"sha256:f6eb3589d952604396c173f3a132039ec1cedbbc57b65f184e1ca67bee914b6b/papers/short.json/support/0.3.1/f9c8348dc1f401cbae8afaedd41f18345751689e6b6298e453c9c48169cf6257"},{"roles":["mapped_claim"],"stage":"expository","subgraph_ref":"sha256:0e0b8ed54de434b100596a9e6374160bfb146bc7905b31307a73825c7034dd44/papers/expository.json/support/0.3.1/f7125c873525eba045c0c24a8bb99ad310a22459dfeb43eb1884a5c1dd02931f"}],"record_ref":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/nodes/quartic.theorem-1"}}]